*Heading
abq2ccx validation: BCs on rigid-coupling members that the reference node's own BCs
impose (an overconstraint Abaqus resolves; ccx stops: dependent side of a MPC and a SPC).
Three 4 x 1 x 1 C3D8 bars clamped at x = 0, in one NLGEOM step:
 A: end face kinematically coupled to RP 1001, which may only move along z; the end
    face also has u1 = u2 = 0 (redundant). Load -1 along z on the RP.
 B: the same bar without the coupling: end face u1 = u2 = 0 and *EQUATION
    u3 = u3(node 177), its centre; load -1 along z on node 177. Must match A exactly.
 C: end face coupled to RP 1003, which may slide in x-y and turn about z (u3 = 0,
    rotations about x and y fixed); the end face also has u3 = 0 (redundant: a
    rotation about z leaves z alone, at any angle). Moment 12 about z, force 3 along x.
